-- Rust binding for anthill.kernel. Proposal 038.
--
-- WI-20260922-BRT4Y: `struct_eq` (`===`) is a kernel operation an OPERATION BODY
-- evaluates, so it has an eval-side host function; registered by hardcoded qualified
-- name in `eval/builtins.rs` until that ticket. `not` is the other (WI-20260923-9R5HN):
-- `anthill.kernel.not(q)` over a reified goal runs a one-shot NAF search, registered by
-- qualified name in anthill-stl until this block named it. Both keep their RESOLVER
-- primitive — the goal reading, `BuiltinTag::Eq` / `BuiltinTag::Not` — which this
-- mapping does not touch. The kernel's remaining body-less declarations (`unify`,
-- `push_choice`, `domain_member`, …) are resolver primitives only, with no eval face, so
-- they have no `operation_map` entry and claim no `@[host_implemented]`.
--
-- NAMESPACE-LEVEL, like most of `anthill.reflect`'s surface: see that binding for why a
-- namespace is a legitimate `operation_map` target (the clause says which host function
-- REALIZES a declared operation; §8.7's rule about provision backing is not in play).
namespace anthill.kernel
  provides anthill.kernel language rust
    artifact "rustland/anthill-core/src/eval/builtins.rs"
    operation_map {
      struct_eq: "kernel_struct_eq"
    }
  end
  provides anthill.kernel language rust
    artifact "rustland/anthill-core/src/eval/reflect_builtins.rs"
    operation_map {
      not: "kernel_not"
    }
  end
end
